{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018r1TXpRPQu7Rqk2yPH8geu","type":"tool_result","content":"## Bugfixes\n- Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir).\n- Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.\n- Also apply the path-separator diagnostic to `--and` patterns, which are matched against file names just like the primary pattern.\n- Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty).\nfmt-ok\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: CHANGELOG.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f955e374-1120-4cee-93cd-a369d4e5dfdb","uuid":"97fb7e40-0b4a-4f30-a7b2-d8cc70959edd","timestamp":"2026-10-18T17:57:29.354Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Bugfixes\n- Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir).\n- Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.\n- Also apply the path-separator diagnostic to `--and` patterns, which are matched against file names just like the primary pattern.\n- Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty).\nfmt-ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: CHANGELOG.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/tmp/tlw-zigdkcq4/CHANGELOG.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":7,"oldLines":6,"newStart":7,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## Bugfixes"," - Handle invalid working directories gracefully when using `--full-path`, see #1900 (@Xavrir)."," - Fire the \"search pattern contains a path separator\" diagnostic for any pattern containing `/`, not just patterns that happen to name an existing directory. Preserves the legacy Windows behaviour that also flags native `\\` separators when the pattern resolves to a real directory. See #1873.","+- Also apply the path-separator diagnostic to `--and` patterns, which are matched against file names just like the primary pattern."," - Fix bug where passing \"-\" as a directory argument didn't actually search that directory, see #849 (@Sean-Kenneth-Doherty)."," "," # 10.4.2"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/tmp/tlw-zigdkcq4/CHANGELOG.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018r1TXpRPQu7Rqk2yPH8geu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgA8oFFUz5TiZ112tvZ2e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`fd` now gives the \"contains a path-separation character\" error for `--and` patterns too, not just the primary pattern. For example, `fd foo --and one/two` used to return nothing silently; now it names `'one/two'` in the error.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `src/main.rs`: `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` now runs the same check over the primary pattern and then each `--and` pattern, and errors on the first one that fails. The check itself is unchanged, including the skip for `--full-path` and the Windows `\\`-plus-existing-directory rule.\n- `tests/tests.rs`: added `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`.\n- `CHANGELOG.md`: one line under Unreleased → Bugfixes.\n\nI chose this over writing a separate check for `--and`, which would have duplicated the logic. The diff is mostly re-indentation.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The new test failed before the fix with no error output, passes after it, and fails again if I revert only `src/main.rs`.\n- The full suite passes: 139 unit and 111 integration tests.\n- `cargo fmt --check` passes, and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` on `src` exits with 0.\n\n**Not run or not touched:**\n- The Windows branch wasn't compiled, since this is a Linux machine.\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets` reports 14 \"redundant reference in `format!`\" errors in `tests/tests.rs`. A clean checkout has 15, so these were already there and I left them alone.\n- When the bad pattern comes from `--and`, the error's suggested fix (`fd . '<pattern>'`) fits less well. The message is unchanged.\n\nNothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":43876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":436,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":578,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f955e374-1120-4cee-93cd-a369d4e5dfdb","uuid":"bd03c9ac-3df1-4e14-b5bd-d7f008aa7383","timestamp":"2026-10-18T17:57:35.289Z","request_id":"req_011CgA8oF2Lj8Soq6NniNgfy"}
